# What must not travel to Vercel.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# `vercel --prod` failed on 2026-09-07 with "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)"
# after uploading 322 MB. The offender was `scripts/tmp/digital-editions/`, the
# staging directory `build-digital-editions.mjs` writes into: Codex Bestiarium's
# master is 109 MB and Vercel's per-file ceiling is 100. That directory is in
# `.gitignore`, which the CLI does not read.
#
# ⭑ EVERY PATTERN HERE IS ROOT-ANCHORED, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT ⭑
#
# The first version of this file wrote `images/` and `assets/` without the
# leading slash. A pattern with no leading slash matches AT ANY DEPTH, so
# `images/` excluded the 25 MB of root-level mockups it was aimed at AND
# `public/images/` — 159 files: every book cover, every category card, every
# preview page. The site deployed with a working catalogue and no pictures, and
# `assets/` had quietly taken `scripts/assets/` with it.
#
#     A path in a deploy-ignore file is a PREFIX, not a directory, unless you
#     anchor it. The check that would have caught this is fetching one image
#     from production, not reading the HTML that references it.
#
# So: fetch an image, not a page, when verifying a deploy.
/scripts/tmp/
/docs/
/images/
/assets/
/e-book/
/sub-pr-report/
/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
